<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 1.2 pct in September - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 1.2 pct in September - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 1.47 billion zlotys, or 1.2 percent, in September to 123.23 billion after a 1.8 percent (revised up from 1.7 percent) rise in August, preliminary central bank figures showed.  </p>
<p>Broad money grew 18.2 percent in the January-September period against 22.4 percent in the same period of last year.</p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		  SEPTEMBER   AUGUST     SEPT 95</p>
<p>  change (pct)			    1.2     1.8   (1.7)    1.2</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		 123.23  121.76(121.63)  94.59</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)    22.39   22.09	    20.77</p>
<p>  National currency		   100.84   99.67 (99.54)  73.81</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		  23.02   23.05 (23.04)  18.01</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector  70.57   67.77 (67.78)  51.84</p>
<p>NOTE: Revised figures in brackets.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
